01:02:15.058 --> 01:02:20.058
You must celebrate a festival for me for seven days.

255
01:02:20.058 --> 01:02:22.058
I always found it so fun as a child.

256
01:02:22.058 --> 01:02:24.058
Then I thought, yes, we are going to build a hut.

257
01:02:24.058 --> 01:02:28.058
We often went for walks in the woods with my parents.

258
01:02:28.058 --> 01:02:30.058
And then I would build a hut.

259
01:02:30.058 --> 01:02:34.058
And I always had to think about that, that I was building a hut.

260
01:02:35.058 --> 01:02:39.058
You must live in those huts for seven days.

261
01:02:39.058 --> 01:02:42.058
That didn't go with my hut in the woods.

262
01:02:43.058 --> 01:02:45.058
That didn't work out.

263
01:02:45.058 --> 01:02:50.058
You must live in them, you who have built them from branches with leaves.

264
01:02:50.058 --> 01:02:55.058
All people born in Israel must live in those booths.

265
01:02:55.058 --> 01:03:06.058
So you and your families after you will remember that I made the Israelites, the people of Israel, live in booths.

266
01:03:06.058 --> 01:03:10.058
When I freed them from Egypt.

267
01:03:10.058 --> 01:03:12.058
I am your Lord.

268
01:03:12.058 --> 01:03:14.058
What does it say here?

269
01:03:14.058 --> 01:03:19.058
When I think of this, I think of such a small hut that I built myself in the woods.

270
01:03:19.058 --> 01:03:22.058
Where it naturally rains completely through.

271
01:03:22.058 --> 01:03:25.058
And where you cannot live at all.

272
01:03:25.058 --> 01:03:33.058
But the people of Israel lived in slavery and oppression in Egypt.

273
01:03:33.058 --> 01:03:35.058
For 400 years.

274
01:03:35.058 --> 01:03:41.058
Until at a certain moment God freed them in a mighty way from Egypt.

275
01:03:42.058 --> 01:03:45.058
I mean, how do you free millions of people from a country?

276
01:03:45.058 --> 01:03:47.058
That is already a miracle in itself.

277
01:03:47.058 --> 01:03:50.058
And he frees them from the land.

278
01:03:50.058 --> 01:03:55.058
They travel through the desert and live all that time in booths and tents.

279
01:03:55.058 --> 01:03:59.058
When they finally arrived in the promised land.

280
01:03:59.058 --> 01:04:01.058
The land that God has given them.

281
01:04:01.058 --> 01:04:08.058
God said, yes but now I want you to set aside seven days each year.

282
01:04:08.058 --> 01:04:10.058
To keep it separate.

283
01:04:10.058 --> 01:04:13.058
That is a designated piece.

284
01:04:13.058 --> 01:04:16.058
Then you build that hut and you will live in it.

285
01:04:16.058 --> 01:04:20.058
You do not stay in your own beautiful house made of bricks.

286
01:04:20.058 --> 01:04:22.058
But you will live in that hut.

287
01:04:22.058 --> 01:04:26.058
Why? To remember who God is.

288
01:04:26.058 --> 01:04:31.058
To remember that God has freed them from that slavery.

289
01:04:31.058 --> 01:04:33.058
From that oppression.

290
01:04:33.058 --> 01:04:39.058
So you could say brought from the old land into the new land.

291
01:04:40.058 --> 01:04:42.058
What did that love hut mean?

292
01:04:42.058 --> 01:04:45.058
Because I always found it just very romantic and very funny and very nice.

293
01:04:45.058 --> 01:04:48.058
But that love hut had depth.

294
01:04:48.058 --> 01:04:50.058
It had meaning.

295
01:04:50.058 --> 01:04:52.058
Commemoration.

296
01:04:52.058 --> 01:04:54.058
From the old to the new.

297
01:04:54.058 --> 01:04:58.058
The realization that God protects you.

298
01:04:58.058 --> 01:05:00.058
Wherever you are.

299
01:05:00.058 --> 01:05:02.058
Whatever you go through.

300
01:05:02.058 --> 01:05:07.058
That people of Israel were truly beaten and oppressed.

301
01:05:07.058 --> 01:05:09.058
They were in slavery.

302
01:05:09.058 --> 01:05:14.058
So it's not just that they worked there as migrant workers.

303
01:05:14.058 --> 01:05:16.058
No, they were in slavery.

304
01:05:16.058 --> 01:05:18.058
And God delivered them from that.

305
01:05:18.058 --> 01:05:22.058
So God protects you no matter what you go through.

306
01:05:22.058 --> 01:05:24.058
And there was something else.

307
01:05:24.058 --> 01:05:27.058
Namely to honor God together with your family.

308
01:05:27.058 --> 01:05:29.058
Together with your family.

309
01:05:29.058 --> 01:05:30.058
With your friends.

310
01:05:30.058 --> 01:05:33.058
To honor God and put Him first.

311
01:05:34.058 --> 01:05:38.058
To leave everything behind for a moment.

312
01:05:38.058 --> 01:05:40.058
The routine of everyday life.

313
01:05:40.058 --> 01:05:43.058
To specifically put Him in the first place for a moment.

314
01:05:43.058 --> 01:05:46.058
Together with your friends and family.

315
01:05:46.058 --> 01:05:49.058
You weren't there alone in such a hut.

316
01:05:49.058 --> 01:05:52.058
So those huts must have been quite large as well.

317
01:05:52.058 --> 01:05:55.058
And they must have been equipped with all sorts of comforts.

318
01:05:55.058 --> 01:06:02.058
Together you come to celebrate for God.

319
01:06:03.058 --> 01:06:11.058
And this is therefore the precursor from the Old Testament to the New Testament.

320
01:06:11.058 --> 01:06:14.058
Because I have always thought, nice such a hut.

321
01:06:14.058 --> 01:06:16.058
But what am I supposed to do with that?

322
01:06:16.058 --> 01:06:20.058
Of course, as a child, you just don't always know the depth.

323
01:06:20.058 --> 01:06:25.058
Or the deeper meanings of what is in the Old Testament.

324
01:06:25.058 --> 01:06:29.058
And what the New Testament means by that.

325
01:06:29.058 --> 01:06:32.058
But let's take a look in the New Testament.

326
01:06:32.058 --> 01:06:36.058
Because what we always think.

327
01:06:36.058 --> 01:06:38.058
Here it comes.

328
01:06:38.058 --> 01:06:42.058
We think that Jesus was born in a stable.

329
01:06:42.058 --> 01:06:45.058
That is nowhere in the Bible.

330
01:06:45.058 --> 01:06:48.058
I looked it up again in the past few days.

331
01:06:48.058 --> 01:06:51.058
It's not there anywhere.

332
01:06:51.058 --> 01:06:54.058
The only thing that is said is.

333
01:06:54.058 --> 01:06:57.058
There was no room for him in the inn.

334
01:06:57.058 --> 01:07:00.058
Was that because the inn was simply full?

335
01:07:00.058 --> 01:07:02.058
Undoubtedly.

336
01:07:02.058 --> 01:07:06.058
But inns, as you know, were also just public places.

337
01:07:06.058 --> 01:07:09.058
Where everyone slept together in one hall.

338
01:07:09.058 --> 01:07:12.058
Just like a hostel today.

339
01:07:12.058 --> 01:07:14.058
Just large dormitories.

340
01:07:14.058 --> 01:07:20.058
There is no place for Mary to bring a child into the world.

341
01:07:20.058 --> 01:07:23.058
So that can't be right, can it?

342
01:07:23.058 --> 01:07:25.058
Even today we wouldn't do that, would we?

343
01:07:25.058 --> 01:07:28.058
Then we would just say, come on, let's set you apart for a bit.

344
01:07:28.058 --> 01:07:31.058
Because there isn't much privacy here.

345
01:07:31.058 --> 01:07:37.058
So at the moment that Joseph and Mary went to Bethlehem.

346
01:07:37.058 --> 01:07:39.058
To register themselves.

347
01:07:39.058 --> 01:07:41.058
This sounds like a Christmas sermon.

348
01:07:41.058 --> 01:07:43.058
But it's coming, don't worry.

349
01:07:43.058 --> 01:07:46.058
At the moment they registered themselves.

350
01:07:46.058 --> 01:07:49.058
It was the Feast of Tabernacles.

351
01:07:49.058 --> 01:07:52.058
Most likely.

352
01:07:52.058 --> 01:07:55.058
It may not be completely 100% clear.

353
01:07:55.058 --> 01:08:01.058
But you see so many references from the Old Testament to the New Testament.

354
01:08:01.058 --> 01:08:04.058
To so many comparisons.

355
01:08:04.058 --> 01:08:07.058
Things that were foretold in the Old Testament.

356
01:08:07.058 --> 01:08:11.058
That at that moment become so clearly true.

357
01:08:11.058 --> 01:08:14.058
That you can actually accept that with certainty.

358
01:08:14.058 --> 01:08:18.058
Jesus was born in a tabernacle.

359
01:08:19.058 --> 01:08:22.058
So at the moment they arrive there.

360
01:08:22.058 --> 01:08:25.058
And knock and say, she has to give birth.

361
01:08:25.058 --> 01:08:27.058
Yes, that's not going to work here.

362
01:08:27.058 --> 01:08:29.058
But wait a minute.

363
01:08:29.058 --> 01:08:31.058
I have already prepared my booth.

364
01:08:31.058 --> 01:08:34.058
Because next week is the Feast of Tabernacles.

365
01:08:34.058 --> 01:08:37.058
And then we would already be living in that booth.

366
01:08:37.058 --> 01:08:39.058
So you can certainly go in there.

367
01:08:39.058 --> 01:08:41.058
It is completely ready to go.

368
01:08:41.058 --> 01:08:47.058
And then, of course, there are many more beautiful, deeper comparisons to be drawn.

369
01:08:47.058 --> 01:08:50.058
But that's for another time.

370
01:08:50.058 --> 01:08:55.058
Those people with the booth.

371
01:08:55.058 --> 01:08:57.058
They had prepared it.

372
01:08:57.058 --> 01:09:02.058
With hospitality in mind, the Jewish hospitality.

373
01:09:02.058 --> 01:09:08.058
To celebrate those feasts with family and friends.

374
01:09:08.058 --> 01:09:10.058
Not just by yourself.

375
01:09:10.058 --> 01:09:12.058
But together with the rest.

376
01:09:12.058 --> 01:09:14.058
Together with others.

377
01:09:14.058 --> 01:09:16.058
So you can kind of imagine it.

378
01:09:16.058 --> 01:09:19.058
I also love organizing parties, of course.

379
01:09:19.058 --> 01:09:22.058
But then you're already busy in your head.

380
01:09:22.058 --> 01:09:24.058
You go grocery shopping.

381
01:09:24.058 --> 01:09:28.058
You think, that one comes, that one loves this and that drink.

382
01:09:28.058 --> 01:09:31.058
And that one comes, that one loves that specific candle.

383
01:09:31.058 --> 01:09:35.058
And so you have people in your mind, family in your mind.

384
01:09:35.058 --> 01:09:38.058
Of whom you think, I want to be hospitable to them.

385
01:09:38.058 --> 01:09:43.058
And I will make a place where we can honor God together.

386
01:09:43.058 --> 01:09:46.058
Where we can celebrate together.

387
01:09:48.058 --> 01:09:53.058
And that Jewish hospitality is held in very high regard.

388
01:09:53.058 --> 01:09:58.058
It cannot be that everyone just sent Mary away.

389
01:09:58.058 --> 01:10:00.058
You wouldn't do that today either.

390
01:10:00.058 --> 01:10:04.058
With someone who comes along with such a belly and says, I am having contractions.

391
01:10:04.058 --> 01:10:06.058
Yeah, goodbye, I have no space.

392
01:10:06.058 --> 01:10:08.058
You don't do that.

393
01:10:08.058 --> 01:10:11.058
So this is really the most logical thing.

394
01:10:11.058 --> 01:10:16.058
And there in that booth, Jesus was born.

395
01:10:18.058 --> 01:10:24.058
The purpose of the booth was to celebrate the liberation from Egypt.

396
01:10:25.058 --> 01:10:34.058
And there in that booth, where you celebrate liberation, the liberator is born.

397
01:10:35.058 --> 01:10:46.058
What that indicates is, what is indicated there as tradition, custom, feast, institution.

398
01:10:46.058 --> 01:10:50.058
The Bible literally says, God's holy days.

399
01:10:50.058 --> 01:10:53.058
This was a highlight for him.

400
01:10:53.058 --> 01:10:57.058
Why? Because he knew he was going to be born in that booth.

401
01:10:58.058 --> 01:11:04.058
Thanking for a new life after Egypt.

402
01:11:04.058 --> 01:11:08.058
Thanking for a new life in a new land, in freedom.

403
01:11:08.058 --> 01:11:15.058
There was an old covenant, or an old way of having a relationship with God.

404
01:11:15.058 --> 01:11:23.058
The people of Israel had to slaughter lambs, slaughter doves.

405
01:11:23.058 --> 01:11:27.058
Did you do something wrong? Off to the temple right away.

406
01:11:27.058 --> 01:11:30.058
To the tabernacle, when they were still wandering.

407
01:11:30.058 --> 01:11:33.058
Just buy a dove, just buy a lamb.

408
01:11:33.058 --> 01:11:36.058
Or did you bring lambs yourself? Just take one along.

409
01:11:36.058 --> 01:11:39.058
As soon as you were healthy, you had to make amends.

410
01:11:39.058 --> 01:11:42.058
You had to have the animal slaughtered.

411
01:11:43.058 --> 01:11:49.058
Then you confess your mistakes and the animal atones for your sin.

412
01:11:49.058 --> 01:11:50.058
That atonement.

413
01:11:50.058 --> 01:11:55.058
That was the old way of having a relationship with God.

414
01:11:55.058 --> 01:12:01.058
Of course, there is now a new way of having a relationship with God.

415
01:12:01.058 --> 01:12:09.058
And precisely in that old covenant, in that old relationship, in the remembrance of that old relationship,

416
01:12:09.058 --> 01:12:12.058
the new covenant was born.

417
01:12:12.058 --> 01:12:15.058
The new Savior was born.

418
01:12:16.058 --> 01:12:20.058
He ensured that we no longer have to slaughter those lambs,

419
01:12:20.058 --> 01:12:24.058
but that he has atoned for our sin.

420
01:12:24.058 --> 01:12:26.058
Forever an eternal one.

421
01:12:28.058 --> 01:12:32.058
He is the replacement of the old agreement.

422
01:12:32.058 --> 01:12:36.058
The replacement of the old rules.

423
01:12:36.058 --> 01:12:40.058
Did he want to tell us that all rules must be thrown overboard? No.

424
01:12:40.058 --> 01:12:42.058
But he fulfills it completely.

425
01:12:42.058 --> 01:12:46.058
We could never meet all those old rules.

426
01:12:46.058 --> 01:12:49.058
But he has done that for us.

427
01:12:50.058 --> 01:12:58.058
You could say, in the memory of the old covenant and the deliverance,

428
01:12:58.058 --> 01:13:03.058
comes the new covenant and the new deliverer.

429
01:13:03.058 --> 01:13:05.058
King Jesus.

430
01:13:08.058 --> 01:13:09.058
Amen.

431
01:13:13.058 --> 01:13:17.058
Old Testament, New Testament, and then the now.

432
01:13:17.058 --> 01:13:21.058
What should we do now? Are we going to build a booth?

433
01:13:21.058 --> 01:13:26.058
Well, who here has a bungalow tent?

434
01:13:26.058 --> 01:13:28.058
I think it's fine, you know.

435
01:13:28.058 --> 01:13:32.058
Who has a trailer or a folding caravan?

436
01:13:32.058 --> 01:13:35.058
Who is going on vacation? Let me ask it this way.

437
01:13:35.058 --> 01:13:38.058
No one? Who is going on vacation?

438
01:13:38.058 --> 01:13:41.058
No one? Who is going on vacation?

439
01:13:42.058 --> 01:13:47.058
Or maybe you just have a vacation and stay here behind the garden. That can also be.

440
01:13:51.058 --> 01:13:56.058
That time to set aside, that's what it's about, with that booth.

441
01:13:56.058 --> 01:13:58.058
We can learn from that.

442
01:13:58.058 --> 01:14:01.058
We can apply that in the now.

443
01:14:01.058 --> 01:14:06.058
For God, that was a high time of days.

444
01:14:07.058 --> 01:14:11.058
To set aside time for a moment.

445
01:14:11.058 --> 01:14:14.058
To get away from the routine of everyday life.

446
01:14:14.058 --> 01:14:19.058
And to be alone with Him for a moment.

447
01:14:19.058 --> 01:14:21.058
Do we do that sometimes?

448
01:14:21.058 --> 01:14:25.058
Just put the phone aside, put the email aside.

449
01:14:25.058 --> 01:14:29.058
Just set an out of office reply. I'm not here.

450
01:14:29.058 --> 01:14:31.058
Just busy with God.

451
01:14:32.058 --> 01:14:34.058
Let's take a look at the now.

452
01:14:34.058 --> 01:14:37.058
Revelation 3, verse 20.

453
01:14:46.058 --> 01:14:50.058
Pay attention, says Jesus. Pay attention.

454
01:14:50.058 --> 01:14:53.058
I stand at the door and knock.

455
01:14:55.058 --> 01:15:01.058
If anyone listens to me and opens the door, I will come in to him.

456
01:15:01.058 --> 01:15:05.058
Then we will eat together, he with me and I with him.

457
01:15:07.058 --> 01:15:11.058
And there comes that hospitality right around the corner again.

458
01:15:11.058 --> 01:15:13.058
Someone is knocking, do you open?

459
01:15:15.058 --> 01:15:17.058
Are you ready to receive someone?

460
01:15:17.058 --> 01:15:21.058
Are you ready to receive Jesus in your life?

461
01:15:21.058 --> 01:15:24.058
Are you willing to let him in?

462
01:15:25.058 --> 01:15:31.058
Jesus says here, I knock on the door, the door of your life.

463
01:15:31.058 --> 01:15:34.058
Yes, how then? What is that?

464
01:15:34.058 --> 01:15:37.058
I mean, those praises, they really built them.

465
01:15:37.058 --> 01:15:40.058
You can hold onto that, it is physically really true.

466
01:15:40.058 --> 01:15:44.058
That Jesus was born is also really true. That is very clear.

467
01:15:44.058 --> 01:15:47.058
But in the now, Jesus is knocking.

468
01:15:47.058 --> 01:15:49.058
Yes, where then?

469
01:15:49.058 --> 01:15:51.058
Not really at your actual front door.

470
01:15:51.058 --> 01:15:53.058
But how then?

471
01:15:53.058 --> 01:15:55.058
What does that look like?

472
01:15:55.058 --> 01:15:59.058
Well, suppose someone tells you about Jesus.

473
01:16:00.058 --> 01:16:04.058
Then you become interested, something stirs within you.

474
01:16:05.058 --> 01:16:09.058
Or you think, uh-uh, I don't want anything to do with that.

475
01:16:09.058 --> 01:16:13.058
Or you actually feel some interest.

476
01:16:13.058 --> 01:16:15.058
You feel a desire.

477
01:16:16.058 --> 01:16:19.058
And you start searching for there is more.

478
01:16:19.058 --> 01:16:21.058
But what then?

479
01:16:21.058 --> 01:16:23.058
You are drawn to it.

480
01:16:23.058 --> 01:16:30.058
And that pulling, that desire, that attraction, that is the knocking of Jesus.

481
01:16:30.058 --> 01:16:35.058
And at the moment when others talk about it, that knocking gets louder.

482
01:16:35.058 --> 01:16:38.058
You feel that something is missing in your life.

483
01:16:38.058 --> 01:16:42.058
You feel that there is a gap in your life.

484
01:16:43.058 --> 01:16:49.058
That desire, that yearning, is already a gentle knock.

485
01:16:50.058 --> 01:16:52.058
And then it gets louder.

486
01:16:52.058 --> 01:16:56.058
And when you cry out, is there more?

487
01:16:56.058 --> 01:16:58.058
Is Jesus knocking harder?

488
01:16:58.058 --> 01:17:00.058
That is the knocking.

489
01:17:00.058 --> 01:17:04.058
That is really quite accurate.

490
01:17:04.058 --> 01:17:06.058
That is not vague.

491
01:17:06.058 --> 01:17:08.058
Doesn't everyone have feelings?

492
01:17:08.058 --> 01:17:12.058
Doesn't everyone have desires or yearnings?

493
01:17:12.058 --> 01:17:16.058
That is therefore very clearly present.

494
01:17:16.058 --> 01:17:20.058
Yes, Jesus is really knocking at your heart.

495
01:17:20.058 --> 01:17:22.058
Really at your life.

496
01:17:22.058 --> 01:17:32.058
And the harder you feel that yearning, or that attraction, the harder He is the one who knocks.

497
01:17:34.058 --> 01:17:39.058
It can be subtle, or it can be getting louder and louder.

498
01:17:40.058 --> 01:17:50.058
But always more and more you long for rest, peace, fulfillment, vision, and purpose in your life.

499
01:17:50.058 --> 01:17:53.058
Those are all little knocks.

500
01:17:53.058 --> 01:17:56.058
And when you say, God, do You know that?

501
01:17:56.058 --> 01:17:59.058
He says, yes, I stand at the door.

502
01:18:01.058 --> 01:18:03.058
So let's take another look.

503
01:18:03.058 --> 01:18:04.058
Very clear.

504
01:18:04.058 --> 01:18:06.058
It is stated here very clearly.

505
01:18:07.058 --> 01:18:10.058
Jesus stands at the door and He knocks.

506
01:18:10.058 --> 01:18:20.058
It does not say, He calls beforehand, or He emails you beforehand, to make an appointment.

507
01:18:20.058 --> 01:18:24.058
And then at the given time, He stands at the door.

508
01:18:26.058 --> 01:18:27.058
That is not what it says.

509
01:18:27.058 --> 01:18:30.058
